12:Ta52,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What time is today Fajr in Delhi (New Delhi)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Today Fajr prayer in Delhi (New Delhi) starts at 5:06 AM (the onset of Subh Sadiq at an 18° solar depression angle) and concludes at Sunrise (6:25 AM). Fasting individuals must cease eating and drinking prior to 5:06 AM."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What time is today Maghrib (Iftar) in Delhi (New Delhi)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Today Maghrib prayer and Iftar time in Delhi (New Delhi) is at 5:47 PM at the precise instant the upper limb of the solar disk sets below the western horizon."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which calculation method is followed in Delhi (New Delhi)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prayer times in Delhi (New Delhi) are calculated using the KARACHI standard with an 18°/18° twilight angle and local latitude/longitude coordinates (28.6139° N, 77.209° E)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between Hanafi and Shafi'i Asr time in Delhi (New Delhi)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In Delhi (New Delhi), Hanafi Asr time begins approximately 45 to 60 minutes after Shafi'i Asr time due to the 2x versus 1x shadow factor calculation. Use our widget toggle above to view both schedules."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is namaz time in delhi hanafi determined for today?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Namaz time in delhi hanafi is calibrated using the 18° astronomical twilight angle for Fajr and Isha, and the 2x shadow length rule for Asr. Masajid across the capital—including Jama Masjid Delhi, Hazrat Nizamuddin, and Fatehpuri Masjid—rely on these verified waqt bounds. For live namaz time delhi today, refer to the interactive timetable above."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the prohibited prayer times in Delhi (New Delhi)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prayer (including voluntary Nafl) is strictly prohibited during three periods: 1) Sunrise until 15-20 minutes thereafter; 2) Exactly at solar zenith (Zawal) for 5 minutes prior to Dhuhr; 3) The 15 minutes before Maghrib sunset when the sun turns pale yellow."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does daylight duration vary throughout the year in Delhi (New Delhi)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Located at latitude 28.6139° N, Delhi (New Delhi) experiences seasonal daylight shifts between the June summer solstice and the December winter solstice. Fasting durations and waqt intervals adjust progressively through each astronomical season."}}]}7:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-10 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$12"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Prayer Times\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com/prayer-times\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Delhi (New Delhi)\",\"item\":\"https://namazeshariq.com/prayer-times/delhi\"}]}"}}],"$L13","$L14"]}]
